# Copy this file to deploy.env and fill in real values before running
# cloudflared/install-cloudflared.sh or radicale/install-radicale.sh.
# deploy.env itself is gitignored (see deploy/.gitignore) -- it holds a
# real domain and tunnel name, but there's no reason to commit those
# either. No secrets end up in this file: the tunnel's own credentials
# are a JSON file cloudflared writes itself (deploy/cloudflared/), and the
# Radicale password is set interactively, never written here.
#
# Order of operations (see deploy/README.md for the full walkthrough):
#   1. Make sure the domain's nameservers already point at Cloudflare (the
#      domain must be an active zone in your Cloudflare account) -- unlike
#      a plain reverse-proxy setup, you do NOT need to create any A/AAAA
#      records by hand; cloudflared's own `tunnel route dns` does that for
#      you as part of step 4.
#   2. cp deploy.env.example deploy.env, edit the values below.
#   3. sudo ./firewall.sh
#   4. sudo ./radicale/install-radicale.sh
#   5. sudo ./nginx/install-nginx.sh
#   6. sudo ./cloudflared/install-cloudflared.sh
#   7. Fill in CC_RADICALE_URL/USER/PASSWORD in /srv/curodav/shared/.env,
#      restart curodav.

# Public hostname for the webapp itself -- and for Radicale, which is
# reachable at https://DOMAIN_APP/radicale/, a PATH under this SAME
# hostname, not a second subdomain. Only one DNS record, one Cloudflare
# Tunnel ingress rule, ever gets created for this app. Local nginx
# (../nginx/) is what splits /radicale/* off to Radicale after the
# tunnel -- cloudflared itself only ever sees this one hostname.
DOMAIN_APP=app.example.com

# Name for the Cloudflare Tunnel itself (shows up in the Zero Trust
# dashboard under Networks > Tunnels). Doesn't need to match either
# domain above -- it's just an identifier for this one server.
TUNNEL_NAME=curodav

# The single Radicale user this app's own CC_RADICALE_USER authenticates
# as, and the same account DAVx5 logs into on the phone -- this is a
# single-user app, one account, not per-viewer accounts. Whatever you set
# here, use the SAME value for CC_RADICALE_USER in
# /srv/curodav/shared/.env afterward.
RADICALE_USER=curodav
